      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E003",
        "passage_id": "P001",
        "quote": "On January 14, 2014, at approximately 8:00 a.m., the plaintiff allegedly slipped and fell on ice as he descended the front steps of the defendants' premises in East Patchogue. The defendants resided at the premises and leased the upstairs unit to the plaintiff. Both the plaintiff and the defendants used the front entrance to enter and exit the property.",
        "statement_status": "allegation"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E004",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "In support of the motion, the defendants submitted, inter alia, the deposition testimony of the plaintiff and the defendant Robert Pucciarelli, which provided conflicting evidence as to the condition of the front steps at the time of the accident, and the defendants failed to establish, prima facie, that they maintained the premises in a reasonably safe condition",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E005",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "Contrary to the defendants' contention, the affidavit of their expert submitted in support of their motion was insufficient to establish, prima facie, that there was no snow or ice on [*2] the front steps at the time of the accident",
